WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.700
Effective configuration management depends on accurate asset inventories and documentation.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:11.160
Organizations need to know what systems exist before they can manage how those systems are configured.

3
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:23.200
Useful documentation may include system owners, software versions, installed components, network relationships, business purpose, approved settings, dependencies, and known exceptions.

4
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:30.840
Documentation supports troubleshooting, audits, security reviews, recovery activities, and operational continuity.

5
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:36.140
It helps teams understand the environment instead of relying only on memory.

6
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.900
Inventory and documentation should be maintained as living records.

7
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.160
When systems change, the records should change too, or the organization loses confidence in its source of truth.
